cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "Crystallize: a two-minute reasoning game about evidence, calibration and replication (SYNTHETIC)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
version: 0.1.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/crystallize"
abstract: >-
  SYNTHETIC educational game, zero dependencies, offline, English and French.
  The player decides how much synthetic data to reveal before claiming that a
  hidden direction exists in noisy 2-D readings, states a probability scored
  by the Brier rule, and faces a simulated reviewer's replication. Includes a
  daily seeded puzzle, a plain-text share card, challenge links and an exact
  Bayesian reference observer for the generator.
keywords:
  - "scientific-reasoning"
  - "calibration"
  - "replication"
  - "scoring-rules"
  - "education"
  - "synthetic"
  - "javascript"
